UPDATE companies SET description='Quantum Semiconductor LLC is headquartered in Santa Clara, California. The company develops a semiconductor technology platform based on atomic-layer engineered Group-IV superlattices that extend silicon''s ability to sense and emit light beyond the visible spectrum.

Its core technology combines Group-IV superlattices (carbon, silicon, germanium, tin, lead) with novel device architectures to produce high-gain, low-noise photodiodes, CMOS image sensors, LiDAR photodetectors, and optical receivers monolithically integrated with CMOS. The platform also enables superlattice heterojunction bipolar transistors for 5G and 6G wireless, as well as quantum sensing, computing, and random-number generation devices. The company holds 27 U.S. patents and 25 foreign patents, with 14 peer-reviewed publications.

The technology targets markets that rely on light sensing and imaging across ultraviolet, visible, and infrared wavelengths. Quantum Semiconductor participates in the Southwest Advanced Prototyping (SWAP) Hub under the Department of Defense''s Microelectronics Commons, indicating defense and aerospace engagement.

The company states its differentiation lies in overcoming silicon''s fundamental optical limitations without requiring heterogeneous integration, delivering noiseless gain in photodiodes and enabling new functionality at minimal added manufacturing cost.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Group-IV Superlattices", "Photo-Diodes", "CMOS Image Sensors", "LiDAR Photodetectors", "Optical/Photonic Receivers", "Superlattice HBTs for BiCMOS (5G/6G)", "Quantum Sensing", "Quantum Computing", "Quantum Communication", "Quantum Random Number Generation", "Atomic-layer engineering", "Epitaxial strain engineering", "Monolithic integration with CMOS"], "industries": ["CMOS Image Sensors", "Optical/Photonic Receivers", "LiDAR", "5G/6G Wireless Communications", "Quantum Sensing/Computing/Communication", "Cybersecurity", "Defense"], "materials": ["Silicon", "Germanium", "Carbon", "Tin", "Lead", "SiGeC", "Group-IV superlattices"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Atomic-layer engineered Group-IV superlattices monolithically integrated with CMOS", "High-gain photodiodes without noise amplification", "Detection and emission from ultraviolet through short-wave infrared", "Single-photon sensitivity for LiDAR at eye-safe wavelengths", "CMOS-compatible process with minimal additional manufacturing cost"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Santa Clara, California -> db", "Technology: Group-IV superlattices, atomic-layer engineering -> /", "Products: Photo-diodes, CMOS image sensors, LiDAR photodetectors, optical/photonic receivers -> /", "Patents: 27 U.S., 25 foreign granted -> /", "Publications: 14 -> /", "Presentations: Semicon West 2024, IEEE Nanotechnology Council 2024 -> /", "SWAP Hub membership under DoD Microelectronics Commons -> /", "Materials: C, Si, Ge, Sn, Pb, SiGeC -> /", "Differentiators: noiseless gain, monolithic CMOS integration, extended wavelength detection -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "unclear", "type_evidence": "Introducing a semiconductor technology platform that significantly expands the function and capability of silicon - revolutionizing what silicon can do with light.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='quantum-semiconductor-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='QuantumScape was founded in 2010 and is headquartered in San Jose, California. The company develops solid-state lithium-metal battery technology aimed at transforming energy storage for a lower-carbon future.

QuantumScape designs and manufactures solid-state battery cells using an anode-less architecture that eliminates the graphite anode, relying instead on a nonflammable ceramic separator. Its Eagle Line pilot production facility in San Jose produces cells for automotive, data-center, aerospace, defense, and consumer-electronics applications. The product lineup includes the QSEV series for electric vehicles, the QSDC and QS PowerBlock systems for AI data centers, and the QSAS platform for aerospace and defense.

The company serves electric-vehicle makers, AI data-center operators, aerospace and defense contractors, and consumer-electronics brands. Its technology targets the need for higher energy density, faster charging, and improved safety in each of those markets.

QuantumScape says its anode-free design reduces material costs and simplifies manufacturing, while the ceramic separator removes the fire risk associated with liquid electrolytes. Removing graphite also addresses supply-chain concerns tied to a single geographic source.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solid-state lithium-metal battery cell manufacturing", "Anode-less cell design and development", "Ceramic separator production", "Pilot-scale battery production (Eagle Line facility)", "Battery technology R&D for automotive, data center, aerospace, defense, consumer electronics"], "industries": ["Automotive", "AI Data Centers", "Aerospace", "Defense", "Consumer Electronics"], "materials": ["Lithium-metal", "Ceramic separator materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Anode-less cell design that eliminates graphite anode", "Nonflammable, noncombustible ceramic separator", "High energy density enabling longer range and runtime", "Fast-charging capability for EVs and data centers", "Secure supply chain by removing graphite dependency"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010 -> db", "Headquarters in San Jose, California -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label) and homepage address", "Eagle Line pilot production facility -> db description", "Anode-less cell design, ceramic separator, elimination of graphite anode -> homepage", "Products: QSEV (automotive), QSDC and QS PowerBlock (AI data centers), QSAS (aerospace/defense/consumer) -> homepage", "Industries served: automotive, AI data centers, aerospace, defense, consumer electronics -> homepage", "Leadership: Pamela Fong, Chief of Human Resources Operations -> homepage", "Social links: LinkedIn, X (Twitter), YouTube -> homepage", "Mission: transform energy storage, higher energy density, faster charging, enhanced safety -> homepage"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "QuantumScape is on a mission to transform energy storage with solid-state lithium-metal battery technology.", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/quantumscape/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='quantumscape' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='R&R Textile Mills Inc. operates from its headquarters in Lombard, Illinois, serving the continental United States. The company has been supplying textile products for nearly three decades, though an exact founding year is not disclosed. It began as a manufacturer and distributor focused on textile solutions for multiple industries.

The company maintains vertically integrated manufacturing across five facilities, with core production in Tamil Nadu, India, and Dhaka, Bangladesh, supplemented by sourcing from China and Pakistan. Its U.S. distribution network includes centers in Lombard, Illinois; Vernon, California; and Wilmington, Delaware. R&R produces cotton-based, microfiber, and synthetic woven textiles spanning kitchen, bath, bedding, craft, and cleaning categories. Food‑service lines include grill cloths, bar mops, aprons, hot pads, oven mitts, dish towels, and napery, while industrial products reach distributors and retailers nationwide. A U.S. fulfillment and processing center provides six service offerings, supported by a technology platform that connects the product life cycle.

R&R serves five primary industries: consumer home, hospitality, healthcare, food service, and industrial supply. Its customer base ranges from healthcare and hospitality distributors to retail chains and restaurant suppliers, with products sold through both internal brands and private‑label programs.

